# Line endings.
#
# Without this file, a Windows checkout converts every tracked text file to CRLF — GitHub's own
# runners have `core.autocrlf=true` — and `gofmt` reads a CRLF Go file as unformatted from line 1.
# The whole lint gate then fails on Windows and passes everywhere else, which is how this was
# found: the first CI run on windows-2025 flagged files that were provably formatted on macOS.
#
# So the rule is `eol=lf` rather than `text=auto`: these files are LF in the repository and LF in
# every working tree, on every platform. Nothing here is edited by a tool that needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries to normalise them.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.car binary
*.dmg binary
*.exe binary
*.jar binary

# Generated and vendored: kept out of diffs and language statistics, but still normalised above.
frontend/pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true
go.sum linguist-generated=true
build/windows/nsis/wails_tools.nsh linguist-generated=true
docs/verbatim/test-inventory.md linguist-generated=true
